WEBVTT

00:02.419 --> 00:03.628
Go!

00:03.712 --> 00:05.005
Kickoff!

00:08.008 --> 00:10.051
You got this!

00:10.677 --> 00:13.096
We have one strength
and one strength only.

00:13.722 --> 00:15.181
An advantage in numbers!

00:15.890 --> 00:19.352
If we keep passing to whoever's open...

00:19.936 --> 00:20.812
There it is!

00:21.396 --> 00:22.272
O-Ogami!

00:25.358 --> 00:26.359
Huh?

00:26.443 --> 00:27.861
He was on the opposite side!

00:28.445 --> 00:29.320
He's fast!

00:33.491 --> 00:35.952
Let's start things off
with a little hello, shall we?

00:36.036 --> 00:37.996
He's shooting already?

00:43.376 --> 00:44.419
Huh?

00:47.422 --> 00:48.298
No way!

00:48.381 --> 00:49.424
He knocked the goal over?

00:56.222 --> 00:58.892
Boss, be careful!
Don't blow your cover with a kick!

00:58.975 --> 00:59.893
Like I care.

00:59.976 --> 01:01.853
I'll worry about excuses...

01:02.353 --> 01:04.731
after I wipe that smug look off his face!

01:14.407 --> 01:15.575
Out of bounds!

01:15.658 --> 01:17.744
Kick-in for the Home Ec team!

01:19.954 --> 01:21.122
Was that for real?

01:21.206 --> 01:22.916
That was actually kinda crazy!

01:23.958 --> 01:26.127
That was way beyond "kinda"!

01:26.211 --> 01:27.670
Tenma's...

01:28.505 --> 01:31.841
kicking power is totally pro-level, but...

01:33.343 --> 01:34.427
Not bad.

01:34.511 --> 01:36.763
Well, I can kick things at least.

01:37.305 --> 01:39.933
Never lost a game
of Kick the Can for distance.

03:09.981 --> 03:13.902
SATURDAY, MAY 16TH

03:15.987 --> 03:18.031
Oh, look at Oga go!

03:18.114 --> 03:22.452
Did he forget that whole "living quietly
and staying under the radar" thing?

03:22.535 --> 03:24.162
Wow, Ogami's incredible!

03:24.746 --> 03:25.955
That was amazing!

03:26.039 --> 03:28.458
Wait, could this actually
turn into a real match?

03:28.541 --> 03:29.626
Huh? Wait.

03:29.709 --> 03:31.794
Oh, I'll take the kick-in.

03:31.878 --> 03:33.212
Thanks.

03:35.173 --> 03:36.382
What's wrong, Shin?

03:39.219 --> 03:40.720
Kohazame?

03:40.803 --> 03:42.639
D-Dude, where's your pacifier?

03:42.722 --> 03:44.182
I-I don't see it lying...

03:44.265 --> 03:45.600
Huh? Sea lion?

03:45.683 --> 03:48.269
Wait, was it when you tried
to block that shot?

03:48.353 --> 03:50.063
Los... Blancos...

03:50.146 --> 03:53.233
Without his pacifier, this guy turns
into a useless bundle of stage fright.

03:53.316 --> 03:54.150
What?

03:54.734 --> 03:58.696
Honestly, I used to be stuck on,
"Why is he always sucking on that thing?"

03:58.780 --> 03:59.948
Right?

04:00.031 --> 04:01.282
Ah...

04:01.366 --> 04:04.202
Must've knocked it loose
when it grazed him.

04:04.285 --> 04:06.204
Do you have a spare?

04:08.623 --> 04:11.626
Um, he says there's one
in his bag in the classroom!

04:11.709 --> 04:12.919
I'll go get it!

04:13.002 --> 04:14.295
I'll go, too!

04:14.379 --> 04:15.755
Thank you!

04:16.381 --> 04:17.423
Fine.

04:17.507 --> 04:20.551
Just stand here for now.
Maybe you'll at least be in their way.

04:21.052 --> 04:24.889
Our advantage is gone!
Now it's just a normal two-on-two!

04:24.973 --> 04:25.890
Hey!

04:25.974 --> 04:28.476
Can we get this game going again already?

04:31.187 --> 04:34.023
He wants you to give him
a lap pillow and pat his head?

04:34.107 --> 04:35.692
That's his dream?

04:35.775 --> 04:37.026
That's what he said.

04:37.110 --> 04:38.820
Why is every single thing
about him so extra?

04:42.699 --> 04:43.783
This guy...

04:43.866 --> 04:45.034
Found it!

04:45.785 --> 04:47.537
Good, it's in a case!

04:47.620 --> 04:49.914
I was worried it might
just be loose in there!

04:49.998 --> 04:51.624
Okay! Let's hurry back!

04:53.001 --> 04:55.920
Although, that pacifier
definitely comes with baggage.

04:56.004 --> 04:56.838
Huh?

04:56.921 --> 04:58.589
Did he tell you about it?

04:58.673 --> 04:59.549
Yeah.

04:59.632 --> 05:01.551
I asked, "Why are you
sucking on that thing?"

05:01.634 --> 05:03.094
That was really direct!

05:03.177 --> 05:05.680
I mean, it'd be weirder not to ask.

05:06.723 --> 05:08.516
I guess because it calms me down.

05:08.599 --> 05:10.393
But if you ask me why...

05:11.185 --> 05:16.232
my mother, who isn't around anymore,
gave me a pacifier with a kind smile.

05:16.316 --> 05:19.235
Only that feeling is still a hazy memory.

05:19.986 --> 05:23.239
Maybe it has something to do with that.

05:23.823 --> 05:26.284
He might have a pretty heavy past.

05:26.367 --> 05:28.453
Maybe you could give him that lap pillow?

05:28.536 --> 05:30.955
I don't think lap pillows
have anything to do with that, right?

05:31.539 --> 05:33.875
Okay, what's happening with the game?

05:35.877 --> 05:37.420
What the heck happened?

05:37.920 --> 05:38.921
Oh! You're back!

05:39.505 --> 05:42.508
Shin's been on fire,
making one god-tier save after another

05:42.592 --> 05:44.010
against Tenma's killer shots!

05:44.093 --> 05:46.304
That's not "on fire"!
He's getting massacred!

05:46.888 --> 05:48.014
Intercept!

05:48.848 --> 05:51.059
This is bad! Noren, get this to him now!

05:51.142 --> 05:51.976
Huh?

05:52.060 --> 05:54.479
If he takes any more of that,
he's gonna die!

05:54.562 --> 05:56.773
Wait, die? But how am I supposed to...

05:56.856 --> 05:57.857
Throw it!

05:57.940 --> 05:59.817
You're probably the best athlete here!

06:00.401 --> 06:02.779
Oh, for crying out loud! What is this?

06:02.862 --> 06:06.032
Shin! New pacifier incoming!

06:06.115 --> 06:07.742
ANPAN

06:14.248 --> 06:15.291
- Huh?
- What the...

06:18.336 --> 06:21.798
Sorry, but things won't go
the way they did before.

06:21.881 --> 06:24.634
I'm quite confident in my footwork, too.

06:24.717 --> 06:25.760
He stopped it!

06:25.843 --> 06:27.929
Is he the same guy as five seconds ago?

06:28.012 --> 06:29.680
- Shin!
- Shin!

06:30.640 --> 06:31.974
All right, let's go!

06:32.058 --> 06:33.518
The real match starts now!

06:33.601 --> 06:36.646
Somehow, you're the only one
who's turned into the fighting type.

06:38.606 --> 06:40.483
- Go!
- You can do it!

06:46.823 --> 06:49.742
That feint's totally basic,
but he's just plain fast!

06:50.618 --> 06:51.744
Dammit!

06:58.835 --> 07:01.170
The change of pace in that split second...

07:01.712 --> 07:03.047
That's it!

07:03.131 --> 07:06.134
The pacifier freak isn't
the only reason Tenma can't score!

07:06.217 --> 07:09.846
This guy looks like a total amateur,
but what the hell is he really?

07:12.849 --> 07:14.100
Out of bounds!

07:14.183 --> 07:16.561
Aw, so close!

07:16.644 --> 07:19.981
That was incredible! Are you getting
better and better as we go?

07:20.565 --> 07:24.193
Well, sure, I do wanna beat Tenma...

07:24.902 --> 07:26.571
but that aside...

07:27.572 --> 07:30.741
Playing sports again
after so long is a ton of fun.

07:30.825 --> 07:33.244
Yeah! Wait, "after so long"?

07:33.327 --> 07:35.204
Sounding too much
like an adult there, Boss.

07:35.288 --> 07:39.208
There's still tension, but it's nice
that nobody's trying to kill me.

07:39.292 --> 07:41.961
Going through trial and error
and keeping up the challenge...

07:42.545 --> 07:43.463
It's kind of exciting.

07:48.384 --> 07:49.677
Hey, Tenma.

07:49.760 --> 07:51.012
Hmm?

07:51.095 --> 07:54.432
The way you keep singling out Ogami...

07:55.391 --> 07:58.436
Is it because deep down,
you're looking for a rival?

07:58.519 --> 07:59.437
Huh?

07:59.520 --> 08:03.441
You were born with that natural physique,
but you never slack off, either.

08:03.524 --> 08:05.401
You're miles ahead
in every sport you play.

08:05.485 --> 08:06.444
Alone at the top.

08:06.527 --> 08:07.612
So, maybe that's why

08:07.695 --> 08:10.114
you're starving for someone
who can actually face you as an equal.

08:10.781 --> 08:11.741
Nah, not at all.

08:11.824 --> 08:12.783
Huh?

08:12.867 --> 08:15.203
I like totally destroying people.

08:15.286 --> 08:17.497
If I could win 100-0, I would.

08:17.580 --> 08:21.000
Wow, I was totally wrong!

08:21.584 --> 08:26.422
I'm doing three sports because I love
all three too much to pick one.

08:26.506 --> 08:29.342
And that whole "alone at the top"
thing you mentioned?

08:29.425 --> 08:30.843
That's actually what I want to be.

08:31.427 --> 08:33.763
Every sport has its legends, right?

08:33.846 --> 08:36.807
And no matter how good
today's players are,

08:36.891 --> 08:39.268
they always get compared to those guys.

08:39.352 --> 08:40.937
That pisses me off.

08:41.020 --> 08:43.856
But what if I leave behind legends
in three different sports?

08:43.940 --> 08:46.108
I'm not talking some soft,
watered-down kind of "unique."

08:46.192 --> 08:49.362
I'm gonna be so one of a kind,
nobody can even argue about it.

08:50.238 --> 08:54.283
He's so far gone, it's almost refreshing.

08:54.367 --> 08:57.370
But if we weren't childhood friends,
I'd stop hanging out with him.

08:57.453 --> 09:01.123
So, yeah, I'm not really looking
for rivals or anything.

09:01.749 --> 09:04.585
But I do have frustrations
from being all alone up here.

09:04.669 --> 09:05.419
Huh?

09:07.088 --> 09:08.756
- Huh?
- What the...

09:08.839 --> 09:10.132
All right!

09:10.216 --> 09:12.760
Yeah! Nice! Now this is getting fun!

09:14.554 --> 09:16.472
I said I like destroying people,

09:16.556 --> 09:18.724
but it's not like
I'm into kicking corpses, you know.

09:18.808 --> 09:21.227
It's just so hard to find

09:21.310 --> 09:24.981
a toy I can play with at full strength
without breaking it.

09:25.690 --> 09:27.066
All righty!

09:27.149 --> 09:29.193
Time to get serious!

09:30.778 --> 09:32.446
He's not bluffing.

09:32.530 --> 09:36.200
I don't think I've ever heard someone say
a cliché like that with a straight face.

09:40.079 --> 09:44.250
People get this wrong all the time,
but when Tenma doesn't go all out,

09:44.333 --> 09:45.960
it's not exactly him playing around.

09:47.086 --> 09:50.756
All he ever thinks about
is improving himself.

09:50.840 --> 09:55.177
And to do that, he never actually
takes it easy on anyone.

09:55.261 --> 09:59.473
But if he overwhelms them too hard
and they give up, that's a problem, too.

09:59.557 --> 10:02.935
So, depending on the opponent,
he limits the kinds of plays he can use

10:03.019 --> 10:04.478
or the area he's allowed to move in.

10:04.562 --> 10:07.982
Basically, it's a self-improvement
challenge run.

10:08.566 --> 10:09.984
You should be proud.

10:10.568 --> 10:14.989
Tenma almost never takes
the shackles off in any sport.

10:23.164 --> 10:26.876
He's only dribbling!
But it's like trying to stop a boulder!

10:28.836 --> 10:29.754
Hah!

10:31.672 --> 10:32.632
Wha...

10:32.715 --> 10:33.466
Wha...

10:33.549 --> 10:34.300
So fast!

10:49.690 --> 10:50.816
Tenma scores!

10:50.900 --> 10:52.318
That's our Superman!

10:52.401 --> 10:55.279
No question about it!
A jaw-dropping three-man breakaway!

10:57.031 --> 10:58.824
And that's the end of the first half!

10:58.908 --> 11:01.494
Tenma's team heads into halftime
with a one-point lead!

11:02.119 --> 11:04.413
That was insane.

11:04.497 --> 11:07.583
I have to admit, even though we're
on Oga's side, that got us hyped, too!

11:08.209 --> 11:10.753
Getting the crowd this fired up
with one play?

11:10.836 --> 11:12.880
That's pure superstar energy!

11:14.340 --> 11:16.467
Even three-on-one isn't enough.

11:16.550 --> 11:17.885
What are they supposed to do?

11:18.969 --> 11:20.763
Would you let me take them by myself?

11:20.846 --> 11:21.597
Huh?

11:22.181 --> 11:23.391
Do you have some kind of plan?

11:23.474 --> 11:25.101
- Nope.
- What?

11:25.184 --> 11:28.521
Well, I'm the one who picked
this fight in the first place.

11:28.604 --> 11:29.897
But never mind that.

11:31.565 --> 11:33.692
Anyway, just let me do this. Please.

11:36.570 --> 11:38.197
- Go!
- Second half is underway!

11:38.280 --> 11:40.741
Does the Home Ec team
have any way to turn this around?

11:41.325 --> 11:42.159
Wait!

11:42.243 --> 11:43.911
Man-to-man?

11:43.994 --> 11:46.414
You seriously think you can beat me?

11:46.497 --> 11:48.457
I'm taking point number two!

11:52.044 --> 11:53.337
I can't shake him!

11:53.421 --> 11:54.422
Why not?

11:54.505 --> 11:56.090
What the hell is going on?

11:56.173 --> 11:58.843
Even if he's got
freakish athletic ability,

11:58.926 --> 12:00.553
how is he keeping up with him?

12:00.636 --> 12:04.515
Is it just me
or does Ogami look like he's...

12:04.598 --> 12:06.142
having fun?

12:07.518 --> 12:10.563
It's not like I've got some chance
of winning, or some big plan.

12:10.646 --> 12:14.108
It's just that, back when
I was really a kid, I hated losing.

12:14.191 --> 12:18.279
No matter how stupid the contest was,
I'd take it seriously.

12:18.821 --> 12:20.698
But the more I grew up...

12:20.781 --> 12:23.617
the less I got fired up about anything.

12:23.701 --> 12:27.246
At work, all that matters
is producing reliable results.

12:27.329 --> 12:30.583
But the more accomplishments
and years I stacked up,

12:30.666 --> 12:33.586
somehow, life just kept
getting duller and duller.

12:33.669 --> 12:36.755
I just remembered how that felt back then.

12:36.839 --> 12:40.384
That feeling of "Like hell I'm losing!"
and going head-to-head is damn great!

12:40.468 --> 12:41.760
Thanks!

12:41.844 --> 12:44.388
Because of you,
I'm having a blast right now!

12:45.764 --> 12:47.433
That's weirdly old-man-ish.

12:47.516 --> 12:48.392
Crap!

12:48.476 --> 12:50.728
But yeah, I agree.

12:50.811 --> 12:53.105
This is what a match oughta be!

12:53.189 --> 12:54.690
And in the end...

12:54.773 --> 12:55.608
I'm gonna win!

12:57.651 --> 12:59.320
This is one hell of a back-and-forth!

12:59.403 --> 13:01.113
- Go!
- Neither one's giving an inch!

13:03.491 --> 13:06.869
Just a minute ago,
he could barely keep up!

13:07.411 --> 13:09.997
There's no way Tenma's losing
in raw physical ability!

13:10.080 --> 13:11.874
Is he predicting Tenma's moves? No.

13:11.957 --> 13:14.043
He's getting a feel for his rhythm.

13:14.126 --> 13:17.505
Whether it's an official sport
or an underworld fight to the death,

13:17.588 --> 13:19.882
one-on-one, the fundamentals are the same.

13:19.965 --> 13:23.260
You identify the exact moment
your opponent will move and match them.

13:31.310 --> 13:32.728
It's a straight-up kicking clash!

13:32.811 --> 13:34.855
I swear I'm gonna win!

13:35.981 --> 13:37.608
They're even on sheer willpower?

13:38.108 --> 13:40.194
No, we are not even!

13:40.277 --> 13:42.738
I'm still holding one hell
of a grudge, you little punk!

13:44.406 --> 13:46.242
Don't look down on the Home Ec Club.

13:46.325 --> 13:48.118
Actually, take a good hard look
at yourself and do better!

13:48.744 --> 13:51.622
Not because it's convenient
for you or whatever

13:51.705 --> 13:54.583
but out of gratitude
for the person who made them!

13:56.627 --> 13:58.546
When someone makes you rice balls

13:59.129 --> 14:01.632
how about giving them a "thank you"?

14:11.517 --> 14:14.270
It's in! Goal!

14:14.353 --> 14:15.312
It can't be!

14:15.396 --> 14:16.313
He got him back!

14:16.397 --> 14:19.191
The Home Ec team comes out
of nowhere with the equalizer!

14:19.775 --> 14:20.818
- Yeah!
- We did it!

14:20.901 --> 14:23.028
All right!

14:30.119 --> 14:33.080
Man, what happened to you?
You actually lost a clash!

14:33.163 --> 14:34.665
Come on, we're getting that point back!

14:44.425 --> 14:45.301
Hey...

14:53.642 --> 14:55.269
I give up.

14:55.352 --> 14:57.229
I can't keep going after that.

14:57.897 --> 14:59.273
I forfeit.

14:59.356 --> 15:00.608
This is my loss.

15:01.191 --> 15:01.942
Huh?

15:03.527 --> 15:04.820
What?!

15:04.904 --> 15:06.989
- What did he just say?
- He's giving up?

15:07.072 --> 15:07.948
That's it?

15:08.032 --> 15:10.200
Give up? Why now?

15:10.284 --> 15:12.536
You're really fine after that?

15:12.620 --> 15:14.872
That's kind of a shock, too.

15:15.873 --> 15:18.250
I hurt myself in that clash just now.

15:18.334 --> 15:20.961
If I push it any further, it'll affect
the sports I'm really serious about.

15:21.962 --> 15:24.048
I'm not looking down on this game

15:24.131 --> 15:27.843
but I only take stupid risks for the
sports I'm actually betting my future on.

15:27.927 --> 15:29.845
I hate it, but I can't continue.

15:30.429 --> 15:31.305
Huh?

15:31.388 --> 15:32.348
We won?

15:33.724 --> 15:35.017
Game set!

15:35.601 --> 15:36.936
For real?

15:37.019 --> 15:38.520
Tenma lost?

15:38.604 --> 15:40.981
Boo!

15:41.565 --> 15:44.777
Yeah, well, with an ending like that,
I can't blame 'em.

15:44.860 --> 15:46.528
Fair enough.

15:46.612 --> 15:48.030
I'll take the booing.

15:48.614 --> 15:49.782
More importantly, Ryohei...

15:49.865 --> 15:51.867
can I lean on you?

15:51.951 --> 15:53.619
Walking's harder than I thought.

15:53.702 --> 15:56.664
What? Dude, you're huge and heavy!

15:57.289 --> 15:58.540
I know.

15:59.583 --> 16:00.793
Hey...

16:00.876 --> 16:03.253
Is the tape in the first aid kit?

16:03.337 --> 16:04.463
Oh... yeah.

16:09.176 --> 16:10.636
Give me your foot.

16:10.719 --> 16:14.598
This isn't exactly my specialty,
but it's better than nothing.

16:14.682 --> 16:15.516
Probably.

16:17.601 --> 16:20.187
The Home Ec Club's president...

16:20.270 --> 16:23.023
Shiraishi. Chisato Shiraishi.

16:23.107 --> 16:24.650
Now the sock, too.

16:25.943 --> 16:27.486
Why?

16:27.569 --> 16:30.489
I still haven't apologized
like I promised.

16:31.115 --> 16:33.200
And besides, I'm the enemy.

16:33.283 --> 16:35.619
What are you talking about?

16:35.703 --> 16:40.708
Jeez, do battle maniacs only see
the world as enemies or allies?

16:41.291 --> 16:45.379
Now, it's true your comments
annoyed me, too.

16:45.462 --> 16:47.423
In fact, I was ready to personally...

16:47.506 --> 16:50.092
But, that's a separate matter.

16:50.175 --> 16:52.428
"When someone's in trouble,
you help them."

16:52.511 --> 16:54.263
That's all there is to it.

16:55.139 --> 16:56.557
There. Done.

17:00.060 --> 17:02.771
That's the kind of club we are.

17:03.313 --> 17:08.652
That said, the fact that you have a clear
dream you're willing to put first

17:09.278 --> 17:12.573
even if it means
getting booed in the moment.

17:13.157 --> 17:15.659
That's worthy of respect.

17:15.743 --> 17:17.202
I borrowed some crutches!

17:17.286 --> 17:18.120
Need these?

17:23.459 --> 17:25.252
Everyone in the Home Ec Club...

17:25.335 --> 17:29.339
I'm saying this not because I promised,
but because I truly mean it.

17:30.674 --> 17:32.760
I'm sorry for making fun of you!

17:33.260 --> 17:35.554
The rice balls you brought were delicious!

17:35.637 --> 17:37.389
Thank you very much!

17:38.098 --> 17:41.894
For better or worse, he is honest.

17:47.149 --> 17:48.067
Hey!

17:48.150 --> 17:49.318
Huh?

17:49.401 --> 17:50.778
Ryo's with you, too?

17:50.861 --> 17:54.156
Yeah, I had a book I forgot to give Ogami.

17:54.782 --> 17:56.742
He should be here soon.

17:56.825 --> 17:57.993
Hey...

17:58.077 --> 17:58.994
Oh, Ogami--

17:59.828 --> 18:01.955
Ogami?

18:02.039 --> 18:03.499
What happened to you?

18:03.582 --> 18:08.754
Well, after all that, people
started recruiting me like crazy.

18:08.837 --> 18:11.965
I mean, you were pretty amazing out there.

18:12.049 --> 18:14.384
Like, not normal amazing.

18:15.636 --> 18:19.264
That was a fluke! You know,
some kind of freak adrenaline rush!

18:19.848 --> 18:21.141
What are you gonna do?

18:21.225 --> 18:23.769
I told you you'd end up
drawing a ton of attention!

18:23.852 --> 18:24.937
What do I do?

18:25.020 --> 18:25.979
Hello!

18:28.065 --> 18:29.066
Huh?

18:29.149 --> 18:29.983
Why?

18:30.067 --> 18:32.111
Tenma Tendo?

18:32.194 --> 18:35.489
Hey, don't look at me
like I'm some kind of ghost.

18:35.572 --> 18:38.992
Don't tell me you've come
to join the Home Ec Club, too!

18:39.076 --> 18:40.160
No, I haven't.

18:40.786 --> 18:43.163
Also, why are you always
sucking on that thing?

18:43.747 --> 18:45.916
There's something I have to do.

18:45.999 --> 18:46.917
Huh?

18:47.000 --> 18:49.086
Well, more like something I want to say.

18:49.169 --> 18:50.462
To you, Chisato.

18:55.008 --> 18:56.552
I've fallen for you.

18:57.094 --> 18:58.929
Please go out with me.

19:02.558 --> 19:03.433
Huh?

19:04.017 --> 19:05.686
What?!

19:05.769 --> 19:08.730
I'm the best when it comes to sports...

19:08.814 --> 19:11.191
but outside of that,
I didn't understand anything.

19:11.775 --> 19:13.777
You made me realize that, Chisato.

19:14.403 --> 19:15.612
And now...

19:15.696 --> 19:17.698
I want to be with you forever!

19:17.781 --> 19:19.616
Wai... Huh?

19:19.700 --> 19:21.201
Hold on!

19:21.285 --> 19:22.661
This sort of thing is...

19:22.744 --> 19:24.913
I'm not used to it, or rather... why?

19:24.997 --> 19:26.790
I'm bad at this, but more like...

19:26.874 --> 19:29.376
How brutally direct
is your approach to life?

19:31.587 --> 19:32.421
Master?

19:32.504 --> 19:34.506
What the hell do you think you're doing

19:34.590 --> 19:37.217
hitting on my precious big sister
out of nowhere?

19:37.301 --> 19:38.385
I'll freaking kill you!

19:38.468 --> 19:40.721
Wait! Are you a
"loves his big sister way too much" guy?

19:40.804 --> 19:46.018
I don't care if you're a Unicorn
or popcorn, I'll grind you into meat!

19:46.101 --> 19:47.436
Calm down, Master!

19:47.519 --> 19:49.730
Tenma! Just get outside for now!

19:49.813 --> 19:51.106
- Huh?
- Just do it!

19:51.190 --> 19:53.609
Master's already
in Thunderclap and Flash stance!

19:56.486 --> 19:58.739
Man, give me a break!

19:58.822 --> 20:01.742
What the hell were you thinking,
making a joke like that?

20:01.825 --> 20:03.744
It wasn't a joke. I'm serious.

20:03.827 --> 20:06.038
Between this guy and Shin...
what is with these people?

20:06.622 --> 20:09.791
Ever since that match, I've been chased
around by every sports club in school!

20:09.875 --> 20:12.419
I can't focus on my school life!

20:12.502 --> 20:16.048
I just want to study quietly
without standing out!

20:16.131 --> 20:17.799
Without standing out?

20:17.883 --> 20:19.176
Quietly?

20:19.259 --> 20:20.344
You want to study?

20:20.427 --> 20:23.263
Right, you're the kind of guy
who wants to stand out, excel,

20:23.347 --> 20:24.598
and doesn't want to study.

20:24.681 --> 20:26.767
That's impossible.

20:26.850 --> 20:28.227
You already stand out.

20:29.436 --> 20:33.565
I don't know what you're hiding,
but it's all gonna come out eventually.

20:33.649 --> 20:35.567
You're the least normal person here.

20:36.276 --> 20:41.073
An amateur doesn't beat me in a clash
by fluke or sheer guts alone.

20:41.156 --> 20:44.826
I've never seen anyone like that
at the top of any sport.

20:49.998 --> 20:51.667
Yeah, you're probably right.

20:51.750 --> 20:56.046
Even without all this,
it might only be a matter of time.

20:56.129 --> 20:58.006
But even so...

20:58.548 --> 21:04.263
I wouldn't trade this peaceful
school life thing for anything.

21:04.346 --> 21:06.139
It's irreplaceable.

21:06.640 --> 21:07.474
So...

21:08.058 --> 21:10.978
I want to keep it going
for as long as I possibly can.

22:44.529 --> 22:47.783
After that, maybe as an apology to me...

22:47.866 --> 22:50.452
he pulled a little string for my sake.

22:51.036 --> 22:53.330
Word got leaked
that Tenma Tendo was injured

22:53.413 --> 22:57.084
and the sports magazines and news sites
were suddenly all over it.

22:57.626 --> 23:00.545
Of course, that wasn't actually true.

23:00.629 --> 23:02.172
The story he wanted spreading was...

23:02.255 --> 23:04.466
"The only reason
Juzo Ogami won was because

23:04.549 --> 23:09.054
Tenma was in nearly
the worst condition of his life."

23:09.137 --> 23:12.015
That took my reputation back down a peg,
relatively speaking,

23:12.099 --> 23:14.059
and the sports club recruiting frenzy

23:14.142 --> 23:16.478
and all the noise around me
gradually died down.

23:17.020 --> 23:18.271
Incidentally,

23:18.355 --> 23:22.317
when I asked him if that meant he'd be
sitting out all the summer tournaments...

23:22.901 --> 23:26.655
I'll just say I got better
and will make a miraculous comeback!

23:26.738 --> 23:27.697
So, there you go.

23:29.783 --> 23:32.035
Worked out great, huh, Boss?

23:32.119 --> 23:35.664
Man, that was close.
I managed to cover it up somehow.

23:35.747 --> 23:36.706
Right?
